      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Exercise test is the first-line tool for the diagnosis of ischemic heart disease. Presently, high technology tests would appear to have lessened the value of this test. We report a case in which ST-segment abnormalities during exercise (ST-segment elevation in leads aVR and V1) allowed us to define the presence and severity of coronary artery disease."},
